From: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: make PMIC GLINK re-registration safe

The PMIC GLINK PDR notifier can unregister and later re-register the same
UCSI instance.  Two error paths make that sequence unsafe:

* pmic_glink_ucsi_register() marks the instance registered even when
  ucsi_register() fails;
* ucsi_unregister() frees the connector array without clearing the pointer.

A later PDR-down event can therefore pass a stale connector pointer back to
ucsi_unregister_port().  This was observed as an osq_lock fault from
pmic_glink_ucsi_register after a failed UCSI re-registration.

Only publish the registered state after a successful registration and clear
the connector pointer when unregistering, so both failed registration and
repeated unregister operations are safe.

Signed-off-by: arch-xiaomi-sheng maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c       | 1 +
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index 7936b391e39e..99c4449a2f79 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -2379,6 +2379,7 @@ void ucsi_unregister(struct ucsi *ucsi)
 	}
 
 	kfree(ucsi->connector);
+	ucsi->connector = NULL;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(ucsi_unregister);
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
index a430af249fee..185e88a99a13 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c
@@ -315,13 +315,19 @@ static void pmic_glink_ucsi_register(struct work_struct *work)
 	struct pmic_glink_ucsi *ucsi = container_of(work, struct pmic_glink_ucsi, register_work);
 	unsigned long flags;
 	bool pd_running;
+	int ret;
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&ucsi->state_lock, flags);
 	pd_running = ucsi->pd_running;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ucsi->state_lock, flags);
 
 	if (!ucsi->ucsi_registered && pd_running) {
-		ucsi_register(ucsi->ucsi);
+		ret = ucsi_register(ucsi->ucsi);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(ucsi->dev, "failed to register UCSI interface: %d\n", ret);
+			return;
+		}
+
 		ucsi->ucsi_registered = true;
 	} else if (ucsi->ucsi_registered && !pd_running) {
 		ucsi_unregister(ucsi->ucsi);
-- 
2.51.0
